    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.test\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nHey 👋 \r\n\r\nI've been experimenting with combining mini.test with busted. The idea is to use the busted CLI to run tests and invoke mini.tests from a `mini_tests_spec` file.\r\nThis allows\r\n\r\n- To use both test frameworks (e.g. busted for unit tests and mini.test for integration tests).\r\n- To use mini.test with our [nvim-busted-action](https://github.com/nvim-neorocks/nvim-busted-action).\r\n\r\nIt works, but I had to [hack into the reporter](https://github.com/nvim-neorocks/busted-interop-examples/blob/d7daad8a564da7eea444dfd6a640db6508d18e5b/mini.test/spec/mini_tests_spec.lua#L8) to make sure I get a non-zero exit code if either of the test suites fail.\r\nOtherwise, a successful mini.test run prevents a failed busted run from exiting with a non-zero code.\r\n\r\nIt would be nice if there were either\r\n\r\n- an API to determine if tests failed \r\n- a possibility to pass in the `quit_on_finish` option as a function that takes the success or failure as an argument (I can see how this might be unergonomic),\r\n  allowing to only quit on failure. \r\n- Or, an option to make `quit_on_finish` a union of `boolean` and `\"on_failure\"`.\r\n\r\nWhat do you think? \r\nI'd be happy to open a PR if you're open to this 😄",
    "closed_at": "2024-08-02T13:34:33Z",
